From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: pass AC-3 and E-AC-3 through AVPlayer

Adds the compressed passthrough sink. On tvOS only AVPlayer renders the
Atmos objects carried in E-AC-3, so spdif-ac3 and spdif-eac3 go to an
AVPlayer that reads the bitstream through an AVAssetResourceLoader
delegate; every other spdif format is still refused, so mpv decodes it.

- ao_avfoundation_iec61937.h and .c turn mpv's IEC 61937 stream back into
  the plain bitstream: burst scanning (data type, payload length,
  completeness), byte swapping, the syncword check, and the stream window
  the loader serves from, with 2 MiB of history kept below the oldest
  reader. Bursts that fail a check are logged and skipped.
- ao_avfoundation_compressed.h and .c run the sink on the output's queue:
  a 50 ms feed timer and a feed step on every loader request, start,
  unpause and tick; filling to compressed-lead ahead of the playhead (twice
  that before it moves), behind the prefetch guard and the window's
  backpressure; the item's clock and the end times mpv takes as its audio
  clock, built from the carrier frames consumed; diagnostics; and the
  fallback that blocks the format for the process and asks mpv to reopen
  audio as PCM.
- ao_avfoundation_compressed_av.m holds AVPlayer (no automatic stall
  waiting, no external playback), a new asset and item for every start
  after a reset, the loader (content type, a 2 GiB content length, no byte
  ranges) and its serving, volume and mute on the player, and
  compressed-buffer as the device buffer.

A start after mpv's end of file resumes feeding the same item and logs
"resuming compressed feed after audio EOF". The sink's logs keep the
formats and levels Vivid reads.

